From 961e9b53b250fe149c343f35436b46272a8554dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RepLog Dev <dev@replog.local>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 06:08:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/15] Session Rating (#10): post-workout 'How was this
 workout?'

Captures a 1-5 subjective rating after each workout to enrich the Training
DNA signal.

- WorkoutSession.sessionRating: Int? added; new MIGRATION_11_12 (DB v11->12)
  adds the nullable column. Migration registered; nullable+default keeps
  backup/restore and existing inserts compatible.
- WorkoutRepository.setSessionRating(sessionId, rating).
- ActiveWorkoutViewModel: WorkoutSummary now carries sessionId; rateWorkout()
  persists the rating (coerced 1-5) and regenerates Training DNA so the signal
  feeds future recommendations.
- WorkoutCompletionDialog: 'How was this workout?' chips
  (Amazing/Good/Average/Poor/Terrible -> 5..1); @OptIn added for FlowRow.
- Migration test: migrate11To12_addsSessionRating + assertColumnExists helper.

Verified: model+domain compile clean on kotlinc 1.9.22 (167 classes); all
references resolve; no conflict markers.
